WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
The scene contains a circle and a square, with the circle on the left.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
The caption “a circle and a square” still fits after their positions are swapped.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.550
That caption lost a spatial relation needed to answer where each object is.

4
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.900
We see a closed, open and closed door at three moments.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.750
Keeping only the first and last frame hides the intervening opening.

6
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.100
Video requires evidence of events between frames, not only of visible objects.

7
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.767
A text query asks for a triangular sign. The archive contains images of three shapes.

8
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:57.617
An aligned system compares text and image representations.

9
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:04.967
The match returns a candidate; its geometry and context still need checking.

10
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:12.317
An image representation can be used to find another archive entry.

11
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:19.167
A generator instead produces a new output conditioned on the request.

12
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:26.517
The first operation retrieves an existing record; the second constructs new content.

13
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:33.867
A table places the twelve-euro amount in the row for order A.

14
00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:41.417
The answer needs the value and its row relation, not just recognition of the number.

15
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:48.767
Keep region, row and document identity so the claim can be checked.

16
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:56.117
A screenshot contains the text of a write request.

17
00:01:56.117 --> 00:02:02.967
Reading the text and proposing a tool are different from executing the operation.

18
00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:10.317
Permission is checked outside the observed content, before the external effect.

